**Actual boundary.** Page joinRoom builds/signs/submits one native membership Join but exposes neither its envelope nor durable retention. ScopeSending/joinAnswers are loaded-Page memory; reload loses the fence. CLI Join already stores its secret-bearing signed envelope privately before submit, retains accepted fact, confirms exact intent/fact/entry, and discovers its own inbox; it is an implementation reference, not a ready browser adapter. Native Join uses invitation authority, expected {}, on:null, invitation number and secret; no pre-Join membership read is assumed. Current ScopeHandle.settle returns Read<Receipt>; not-found is nonterminal, not permission for a new key/signature/invitation.

**One custody owner/path.** Add a private same-origin enrollment module owned by C4/C5. Existing Settings Join and invitationTask must delegate to it and the SAME actual-enrollment fence/maps. No second Join sender. Actual identity is normalized serving origin + full membership reference/incarnation + signing-key ID, independent of currently selected room/settings/invitation. Original full directory reference, native membership hint, rules/destination IDs, invitation handle and credential reference are separately retained and verified. Changing settings, invitation or displayed label never clears an unresolved actual-enrollment record. An invitation handle/ref is a hint until native accepted entry plus current membership/directory readback verifies it.

**Minimal internal API proposal:** split current joinRoom into buildJoin(session, typed) -> private JoinEnvelope {normalizedOrigin, full repository refs, explicit supported native hint, handle, keyId, credentialRef, invitationDigest, signed, grants:[], beside:{}} and submitJoin(envelope) -> Answer. Keep its validation/signing fields identical to current Join; no public wire operation/schema is added. The envelope is an internal value never returned to public status/export/console/URL/artifacts. Existing joinRoom wrapper may delegate through the single custody module; it must not retain an alternate unjournaled mutation path. Status returns opaque operation ID, phase, original nonsecret binding, known native answer/receipt and separate observation; secrets stay private. Build takes an already retained original credential; it never silently generates/replaces a key on resume.

**Private storage and locking.** Use one canonical JSON record per actual enrollment, atomically written and read back through the existing ClaimStorage-style same-origin storage primitive; reuse mandatory ClaimLocks/Web Locks, never the claim record/CLI global store itself. Proposed bounds for review: 64 enrollment records, 16 KiB raw invitation before base64 decode, 64 KiB per serialized record, 4 MiB total journal. Check character/UTF-8 limits before decode/parse without allocating an unbounded byte buffer; strict canonical parsing then exact shape/type/signature/digest validation. Current browser storage is origin-private, not encrypted against same-origin code; no new secrecy promise. A credential ref points to existing private Page key custody and its fingerprint; no second key copied into public metadata. Preserve all unresolved records and their original raw bytes when corrupt/legacy/missing; fail closed rather than drop, evict, overwrite or migrate into a fresh Join. Storage clear/lost credential has no guaranteed browser recovery; report the original enrollment unresolved and defer reenrollment to its authorized owner.

Obtain a Web Lock keyed by the actual enrollment identity BEFORE lookup/build/sign, then re-read the record and original credential after acquiring it. Hold it through saved-stage update/submission/reconciliation/readback; a second tab waits and reloads the first tab's actual record, never signs another Join. Missing lock support stops before mutation. Guard origin and exact credential ID/full refs at every continuation and immediately before POST. The original settings selection is only a presentation context; preserve it rather than auto-selecting a late answer. Origin policy is the Worker's actual location.origin, matching current Page behavior; an invitation to another origin is refused locally without transmission.

**Record and ordering.** Retain v/version, opaque operation ID, original origin/full D/M/native hint/handle/rules/destination, credential ref and key ID, canonical invitation bytes/digest/secret, exact signed intent/digest/native grants/beside, local prepared state (no native preparation API), attempted flag, each full known answer, accepted fact/verified-entry status, current readback observation and explicit selection status. Verify signed actor matches retained credential key; target is exact original membership; kind Join, on:null, expected {}, exact invitation/secret fields, no extra grants/beside. Verify stored native answer variants before using them; malformed refused/accepted records cannot bypass validation. A stored accepted receipt must have exact target incarnation and intent digest; follow native entry and recompute full fact hash/at/seq, verify the signed Join, opening key/member relationship and created inbox. No synthetic acceptance or assumed handle/current authority.

Generate the private device key only for a deliberate NEW enrollment, preserve the user's existing selected context/key, and verify key storage/readback first. Build once under lock; save/read back complete original envelope BEFORE any submit. Persist attempted:true/read back immediately before POST. If either save fails, send nothing new and keep existing records. After reply, save the known full answer immediately BEFORE any awaited receipt/readiness/settings/repaint operation. If post-accept storage fails, keep the answer in memory and original persisted attempted envelope; reload must settle that same request rather than open another enrollment. A key write that succeeded but failed verification is indeterminate local storage, not proof that the old key remains selected.

**Reload/reconciliation.** Restore the original validated record and credential under lock; never regenerate secret, deadline/idempotency key or signature. An attempted record with no verified accepted result first settles the ORIGINAL signed intent. Accepted receipt is retained then followed; unavailable/malformed/lost reply, mismatch, read refusal and not-found keep unknown. Optional deliberate resend uses the same signed/grants/beside bytes and original target ONLY, under current original-key/context guard; no automatic retry loop. Expired/revoked-key resend may refuse but does not erase a previous unknown acceptance. A later refusal is an answer about its judged head; it does not establish terminal absence for an earlier attempted send. If a brand-new submission gets a definite refusal and there was no earlier unknown, keep that refused record/draft; this slice offers no automatic replacement or discard. No universal B2 terminal/preparation API is invented.

After verified acceptance, authenticate room readback using the retained key: directory Summary.scope must equal full original D; its membership reference must equal full M; current standing must identify the invitation's actual admitted member/key, and rules/destination links must match the original repository. Missing/revoked standing is access lost, not erased historical acceptance. Accepted enrollment plus unavailable readback displays **Enrollment recorded; room access unavailable**. Readiness checks activated definitions/rules separately; Join never means app ready. “Use joined room” is explicit and only after authenticated readback; settings write/readback failure leaves the original record recoverable and current selection intact/indeterminate, never submits Join again. Other known enrollments and late answers remain indexed by their actual record, not one overwritable selected-context slot.

**Cancellation/errors.** Cancel before attempted only dismisses local UI; retain privately stored prepared request for inspection unless the owner proves it was never submitted and explicitly discards it. Cancel after attempted cannot undo enrollment or revoke a key; keep unknown/accepted custody. Context changes stop new POSTs but read-only settlement of the original record may continue; late answers are saved to that record, never activate another room/key. Closed tab releases lock; attempted:true makes the next tab/reload reconcile rather than re-sign. Removed/revoked key or cleared credential prevents new mutations and may prevent authenticated room reads; exact accepted history remains retained where native reads permit it. No admin/operator key transfer or inferred same-member recovery. Disable fresh Join for that actual enrollment across UI/redraw/reload until this owner resolves it.

**Smallest implementation after independent authority review:** C4/C5 owner18815307e6c306d63766230ed7eb7ddbf94d1f21 owns private join module/parser/lock/credential adapter; Page data exposes envelope before submit and delegates to it; main Settings and invitationTask share its fence/state/known-result projection; client native settle/followReceipt remains unchanged. No generic outbox, workspace or device-key redesign, installation/founding or new catalog. Existing full C4 two-device enrollment/revocation/same-member recovery/non-extractable key objectives and C5/C6 hosted acceptance remain owed. Review exact storage/API/error semantics before runtime commission; current loaded-Page reload limitation remains until implemented and witnessed.

**Acceptance/control set:** real native Join lost after acceptance then reload resumes exact key/envelope and verifies one member/key/inbox; two tabs race and only one signed request/POST is created; another invitation/settings under same actual unknown identity cannot replace it. Before-POST storage failure or context/key/ref/origin mismatch produces zero mutation; post-answer storage/readback/settings failure preserves accepted result/original proof. Oversized/malformed/wrong-signature/ref/incarnation/intent/answer record blocks before signing/transport; key-clear/revocation reports access lost without fake recovery. Native settle not-found keeps unknown; deliberate retry sends identical original bytes; expired/used/wrong-origin invitations and removed member refuse honestly. Accepted records survive unrelated enrollment/late answers without masking; explicit selection revalidates identity. One meaningful pre-save guard and one lock/envelope reuse control at real boundary, with browser reload/two-tab proof and stand-ins labelled; no protocol/fixture approval masquerades as hosted cold-browser completion. No tests ran for this specification.

